{"paper": "SSC-DelhiPoliceHC-17-Oct-2022-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 20, "tagged_count": 20, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3.34", "added": false}, {"text": "0.00334", "added": false}, {"text": "0.334", "added": false}, {"text": "0.0334", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "4 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "7 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "8 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "3.5 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "What would be the simple interest (in Rs.) of the principal amount of Rs.10,000 for 3 months at a rate of 16% per annum?", "options": [{"text": "200", "added": false}, {"text": "800", "added": false}, {"text": "1600", "added": false}, {"text": "400", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "R", "added": false}, {"text": "S", "added": false}, {"text": "Q", "added": false}, {"text": "P", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "Tom can do a piece of work in 5 days and Jerry in 8 days. They work together but 3 days before the completion of the work, Tom leaves. In how many days was the work completed?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "In a triangle PQR, S is a point on the side PQ and T is a point on the side PR such that STRQ is a trapezium. Given that ST : QR = 4 : 5, what is the ratio of the area of trapezium STRQ to the area of the triangle PST?", "options": [{"text": "16 : 25", "added": false}, {"text": "25 : 16", "added": false}, {"text": "9 : 16", "added": false}, {"text": "16 : 9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "X and Y have their monthly incomes in the ratio 9 : 7 while their monthly expenditures are in the ratio 5 : 3. If they have saved ₹16,000 and ₹14,000 monthly, respectively, then the difference in their monthly incomes is:", "options": [{"text": "₹5,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹7,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹8,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "(4.5 × 4.5 + 22.5 + 2.5 × 2.5) is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "4.9", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "49", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "The average age of 40 girls of a class is 15 years. When the age of the science teacher is included, the average becomes 16 years. Find the age of the science teacher.", "options": [{"text": "46 years", "added": false}, {"text": "56 years", "added": false}, {"text": "45 years", "added": false}, {"text": "55 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "replacement-effect", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "In which set of numbers every pair is coprime to each other?", "options": [{"text": "42, 55, 69", "added": false}, {"text": "21, 32, 43", "added": false}, {"text": "35, 48, 55", "added": false}, {"text": "24, 35, 49", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "A company's workforce shrank from 40 to 29 people. What is the staffing reduction percentage?", "options": [{"text": "30%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "27.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "29.3%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "If a shopkeeper marks up his price by 20% and then allows a 20% discount, what is his percentage profit or loss?", "options": [{"text": "4% profit", "added": false}, {"text": "4% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "5% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "5% profit", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "A person gives 5% and 15% two successive discount on a watch. If the selling price of the watch is ₹323, then its marked price is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "Nita travelled a distance of 57 km in 11 hours. She travelled partly on foot at 3 km/h and partly on bicycle at 11 km/h. What is the distance travelled on bicycle?", "options": [{"text": "38 km", "added": false}, {"text": "33 km", "added": false}, {"text": "24 km", "added": false}, {"text": "29 km", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "A can complete a work in 15 days and B in 20 days. If they work on it together for 4 days, then the fraction of work that is left will be_______.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "Rita invested ₹50,000 in a bank. In two years how much compound interest will she get, if the first-year rate of interest was 10% and in the second year it was 4% more than the first year?", "options": [{"text": "₹12720", "added": false}, {"text": "₹12710", "added": false}, {"text": "₹12690", "added": false}, {"text": "₹12700", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3 pqr", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "If a closed cylindrical tank of radius 1.5m and height 3m is to be made from a sheet of metal, then how much sheet of metal is required to do it to ignore the wastage?", "options": [{"text": "42.42 m2", "added": false}, {"text": "42.24 m2", "added": false}, {"text": "24.24 m2", "added": false}, {"text": "24.42 m2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}]}